<!--
    decbench campaign case, NOVEL pool: O2-tar-tar-xstrcat (filed as
    O2-noinline-iproute2-ip).  58 of 101 sampled binaries and 283 functions
    emitted an identifier containing `$$`, which is not a legal C identifier;
    no other decompiler in the benchmark (angr, ghidra, ida, binja, phoenix,
    dewolf, r2dec) ever emits one.

    P6 variable and storage model, local naming.  `Scope::buildUndefinedName`
    (database.cc:2854) names a Symbol created with an empty name `$$undef` plus
    8 hex digits.  Upstream that string is unobservable: `ActionNameVars::apply`
    renames every still-undefined Symbol before it returns, and `PrintC` reads
    `sym->getDisplayName()` LIVE at emit time, so the render always sees the
    final name.  kuna diverges on both counts.  The name is cached per
    HighVariable (`HighVariable::kuna_name`), and the catch-all rename, though
    ported as `Database::assign_default_names`, had zero call sites.  So the
    placeholder reached the emitted C, the `variables` array of
    `decompile-all` in JSON mode, and the `.asm` stack-frame comments of
    `decompile-project`.

    Both producers are closed at the tail of `name_local_highs_angr`
    (`p6_variables/kuna_undefname.rs`), the same place the port already resolves
    this class of ordering hazard for the spacebase pass:

      * stale cache.  `resolve_default_name_override` renames the covering
        Symbol only for a whole-symbol cover (the C++ `namerec` gate
        `sym->isNameUndefined() && high->getSymbolOffset() < 0`) and otherwise
        returns the Symbol's CURRENT display name.  A partial-cover high visited
        before its whole-cover sibling therefore caches the placeholder, the
        sibling then renames the shared Symbol to `vN`, and nothing back-fills
        the first cache.  The tail re-reads the Symbol once, kuna's stand-in for
        upstream's live `getDisplayName()`.
      * never renamed.  A Symbol no high covers wholly keeps the placeholder in
        the Symbol table itself.  The tail wires
        `localmap->assignDefaultNames(base)`, the final statement of upstream's
        `ActionNameVars::apply` (coreaction.cc:3079).

    Neither step can renumber an existing local: both run after every `vN` has
    been handed out, and the re-read consumes no name index at all.

    No option: an identifier containing `$$` is not valid C under any policy,
    and the split made the body read a name nothing writes.  DIV-58.

    ==== witness 1: the stale cache (tar xstrcat) ====

    Bytes are GNU tar 1.34 (O2, stripped) `xstrcat` at 0x611a0, a varargs string
    concatenator; its five callees are stubbed `ret` at their real addresses.
    The loop is the x86-64 `va_arg` expansion over the caller's `va_list`:

        if (gp_offset >= 48) use overflow_arg_area else reg_save_area+gp_offset;
        gp_offset += 8;

    `gp_offset` is the low 4 bytes of the 8-byte stack slot at stack - 0x58, so
    the slot carries a 4-byte partial high AND an 8-byte whole high.  The
    partial sorts first in location order, so before the fix the guard and the
    bump both read `$$undef00000000` while the induction update landed on `v12`.
    That is a loop testing and incrementing a variable nothing ever writes:

        uint4 $$undef00000000; // stack - 0x58
        uint8 v12;             // stack - 0x58
        ...
          v5 = v12 & 0xffffffff;
          if (0x30 <= (uint4)$$undef00000000) { ... }
          else v12 = (uint8)((uint4)$$undef00000000 + 8);

    The 4-byte high is a strict partial of the one scalar Symbol, so once the
    two agree on the name the printer's existing whole-sibling guard folds the
    duplicate declaration, in BOTH passes: that guard is not part of
    `dedupvardecls`.

    ==== witness 2: the unwired catch-all (iproute2 ip set_qlen) ====

    Bytes are iproute2 6.1 (O2-noinline, stripped) `set_qlen` at 0x2b420 with
    its five callees stubbed and the one string it passes to `perror`.  The
    source builds a single `struct ifreq ifr`; kuna splits the frame into a
    16-byte name buffer plus a 4-byte slot at stack - 0x38 for the union member,
    and NO high covers that slot wholly, so `resolve_default_name_override` was
    never reached for it and the Symbol kept its placeholder in the Symbol table
    as well as in the render:

        char $$undef00000001 [16]; // stack - 0x38
        ...
        $$undef00000001 = CONCAT124(v4[0],a1);

    Wiring `assignDefaultNames` names it after every other local, so it becomes
    `v7`, the highest index in the function, as the ordering guarantees.

    Pass 1 is the default pipeline and asserts the fix.  Pass 2 sets
    `option dedupvardecls off` to pin that neither witness depends on the P9
    declaration collapse: this is a P6 naming fix, so the off path renders
    identically.  Assertion counts span both passes.
-->
